  rationale: The ledger is empty, so round 1 should establish baselines across model families rather than tune anything. Telco churn is a small, mostly categorical tabular problem where regularised logistic regression is often competitive with boosting, so I test a linear baseline, a well-regularised boosting baseline, and a bagged tree baseline. I vary the feature set slightly (raw vs engineered) to get an early read on whether the engineered columns help, keeping class_weight=none and calibration=none so PR-AUC comparisons are clean.
