Round 3 [claude] 3 experiments planned
  rationale: The ledger shows a tight plateau around 0.662-0.666 across four very different families, with no confirmed gains in two rounds; hist_gb with strong shrinkage/shallow depth is nominally best. What remains open is whether heavier regularisation of the boosters (very small trees, more rounds) or a strongly regularised, lower-dimensional model can push past noise. I propose one further-regularised hist_gb on engineered features, one heavily constrained LightGBM (few leaves, feature subsampling) and one minimal-feature logreg to test whether dimensionality reduction helps ranking.
